======================================================================================================================
G2-c  linear perturbation equations of the localised RR model on FRW (sympy) and the quasi-static reduction
======================================================================================================================
    delta E_00      = 2*k**2*m2*Sb(t)*psi(t)/(3*a(t)**2) - k**2*m2*s(t)/(3*a(t)**2) - 2*k**2*psi(t)/a(t)**2 + 2*m2*Sb(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t)/a(t) - m2*Ub(t)**2*phi(t)/6 - m2*Ub(t)*u(t)/6 + m2*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t) + m2*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(u(t), t)/6 + m2*Derivative(Ub(t), t)*Derivative(s(t), t)/6 - m2*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(s(t), t)/a(t) - m2*s(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)**2/a(t)**2 - 6*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t)/a(t)
    delta(E_xx-E_yy)= k**2*(-m2*Sb(t)*phi(t) + m2*Sb(t)*psi(t) - m2*s(t) + 3*phi(t) - 3*psi(t))/3
    delta(box U + R)= 2*k**2*phi(t)/a(t)**2 - 4*k**2*psi(t)/a(t)**2 - k**2*u(t)/a(t)**2 + 2*phi(t)*Derivative(Ub(t), (t, 2)) + Derivative(Ub(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t) + 3*Derivative(Ub(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t) - 6*Derivative(psi(t), (t, 2)) - Derivative(u(t), (t, 2)) + 6*phi(t)*Derivative(Ub(t), t)*Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t) - 12*phi(t)*Derivative(a(t), (t, 2))/a(t) - 6*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t)/a(t) - 24*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t)/a(t) - 3*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(u(t), t)/a(t) - 12*phi(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)**2/a(t)**2
    delta(box S + U)= -k**2*s(t)/a(t)**2 + 2*phi(t)*Derivative(Sb(t), (t, 2)) + u(t) + Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t) + 3*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t) - Derivative(s(t), (t, 2)) + 6*phi(t)*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t) - 3*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(s(t), t)/a(t)
    quasi-static scaling (s = sigma/k^2, phi, psi, u = O(1), k -> infinity):
       E_00:  k^2 coefficient = 2*(m2*Sb(t) - 3)*psi(t)/(3*a(t)**2)   (expected -2 Fbar psi / a^2)
       E_xx-E_yy: k^2 coefficient = -m2*Sb(t)*phi(t)/3 + m2*Sb(t)*psi(t)/3 + phi(t) - psi(t)   (expected Fbar (phi - psi))
       box U + R: k^2 coefficient = (2*phi(t) - 4*psi(t) - u(t))/a(t)**2   (expected (2 phi - 4 psi - u)/a^2)
       box S + U: k^0 coefficient = 2*phi(t)*Derivative(Sb(t), (t, 2)) + u(t) + Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t) + 3*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(psi(t), t) + 6*phi(t)*Derivative(Sb(t), t)*Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t) - sigma(t)/a(t)**2   (u - sigma/a^2 plus S-bar-derivative x (phi, psi) terms of the same order as u, so s = a^2 (u + O(phi, psi))/k^2; an earlier draft of this check expected exactly u - sigma/a^2 and was too strict, corrected before any number was used)
  [PASS] G2-c: the k^2-enhanced (quasi-static) coefficients are exactly  -2 Fbar psi/a^2 (00),  Fbar (phi - psi) (traceless ij),  (2 phi - 4 psi - u)/a^2 (U); the S equation has s = a^2 (u + O(phi,psi))/k^2; Fbar = 1 - m^2 S-bar/3
         symbolic match: True
    => quasi-static:  k^2 psi = -4 pi G a^2 delta-rho / Fbar  (mu = G_eff/G = 1/Fbar),  phi - psi = O(m^2 a^2 u/k^2) (eta = psi/phi = 1 + O(m^2 a^2/(Fbar k^2))),  u = 2 phi - 4 psi,  s = a^2 u/k^2
    neglected terms are the k^0 coefficients (time derivatives of phi, psi, u, s times H, and m^2 u, m^2 U-bar^2 phi): relative size O((a H/k)^2) and O(m^2 a^2/k^2).

